WEBVTT

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.976
you make observations, you know.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.976
And then you slowly build up a theory

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.976
of how this stuff works.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.096
And it was --
I was following all the rules.

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:09.976
I didn't know what the rules were,

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.976
I'm a natural born scientist, I guess,

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.976
or some kind of a throwback
to the 17th century, whatever.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.976
But at any rate, we finally did

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:20.976
have a device that would reproduceably

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.976
put a frog out of sight

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.976
and get him back alive.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.976
And we had not --

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.976
I mean, we weren't frightened by it.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.429
We should have been,
because it made a lot of smoke